[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m Let's represent \(z\) in polar form. Since \(|z| = 4\), we can write \(z = 4e^{i\theta}\), where \(\theta\) is a real number. This means \(z = 4(\cos \theta + i \sin \theta)\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m Now, we can substitute \(z = 4e^{i\theta}\) into the expression:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m (75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z} = (75 + 117i)4e^{i\theta} + \frac{96 + 144i}{4e^{i\theta}}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m Simplifying the expression, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m (75 + 117i)4e^{i\theta} + \frac{96 + 144i}{4e^{i\theta}} = 4(75 + 117i)e^{i\theta} + \frac{96 + 144i}{4}e^{-i\theta}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m This can be written as:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m 4(75 + 117i)(\cos \theta + i \sin \theta) + \frac{96 + 144i}{4}(\cos \theta - i \sin \theta).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m Expanding this, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m 4(75 \cos \theta + 117i \cos \theta + 75i \sin \theta - 117 \sin \theta) + \frac{96 \cos \theta + 144i \cos \theta + 96i \sin \theta - 144 \sin \theta}{4}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m Combining real and imaginary parts, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m 4(75 \cos \theta - 117 \sin \theta) + 4i(117 \cos \theta + 75 \sin \theta) + \frac{96 \cos \theta - 144 \sin \theta}{4} + \frac{144 \cos \theta - 96 \sin \theta}{4}i.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m Combining the real and imaginary parts, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m 4(75 \cos \theta - 117 \sin \theta) + \frac{96 \cos \theta - 144 \sin \theta}{4} + \left(4(117 \cos \theta + 75 \sin \theta) + \frac{144 \cos \theta - 96 \sin \theta}{4}\right)i.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m The real part of this expression is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m 4(75 \cos \theta - 117 \sin \theta) + \frac{96 \cos \theta - 144 \sin \theta}{4}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m Combining the terms, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m 4(75 \cos \theta - 117 \sin \theta) + \frac{96 \cos \theta - 144 \sin \theta}{4} = 300 \cos \theta - 468 \sin \theta + 24 \cos \theta - 36 \sin \theta = 324 \cos \theta - 504 \sin \theta.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3430201)[0m To maximize \(324 \cos \theta - 504 \sin \theta\), we can use the fact that the maximum value of \(a \cos \theta + b \sin \theta\) is \(\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\). Here, \(a = 324\) and \(b = -504\), so the maximum value is:
